{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-indent: -18pt;&quot;&gt;The proposal fails to provide a sufficient number of car parking spaces within the curtilage of the site and furthermore their size are insufficient to accommodate a standard\r\nvehicle, rendering them unusable for their intended purpose. The proposal&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-indent: -24px;&quot;&gt;would fail to provide a sufficient level of parking to meet the needs of future occupiers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-indent: -18pt;&quot;&gt;, resulting in an increase in the demand for on-street parking, to the detriment\r\nof highway safety and the free flow of traffic. The proposal is therefore\r\ncontrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policy CS1 of the\r\nHarrow Core Strategy (2012), Policies DM1, DM26 and DM43 of the Harrow Development\r\nManagement Policies Local Plan (2013) and Policy T6.1 of the London Plan\r\n(2021).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;The living/kitchen area within proposed Flat 2\r\nwould have only one opening providing its only source of light\r\nand outlook, which would directly face the proposed boundary fence adjacent to\r\nFlats 1 and 2. The light and outlook to this habitable room would\r\ntherefore be inadequate for future occupiers and would result in a\r\nperception of a loss of privacy between Flat 2 and the private\r\namenity space for Flat 1. &amp;nbsp;The proposal therefore fails to provide a high\r\nstandard of residential accommodation for future occupiers and is therefore contrary to the\r\nhigh-quality design aspirations of the National Planning Policy Framework\r\n(2024), Policy D3(D7) and D6 of The London Plan (2021) and Policies DM1 and\r\nDM26 of the Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013) and the\r\nResidential Design Guide SPD (2010).&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;The proposal, by reason of the fragmented and\r\ncontrived subdivision of the rear garden, would fail to provide a practical, or\r\nhigh-quality arrangement of private amenity space for future occupiers and results in a refuse area which is inconvenient for future occupiers due to its siting and convoluted access.&amp;nbsp; As such, the development is contrary to the National\r\nPlanning Policy Framework (2024), Policies D3(D7), D3(D10) and D6 of the London\r\nPlan (2021), Policies DM1, DM26 and DM27 of the Harrow Development Management\r\nPolicies Local Plan (2013), the Residential Design Guide SPD (2010) and the\r\nHousing Design Standards LPG (2023).&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
